# Design review checklist

When finishing a UI change, run this pass (use `web-design-guidelines` + `accessibility` + `web-quality-audit` skills for depth):

- [ ] Brand test: first viewport still reads as Oriana without the nav
- [ ] No generic AI look (purple gradients, Inter/Roboto defaults, cream+terracotta, glow pills)
- [ ] Hierarchy: one primary CTA; secondary actions quieter
- [ ] Spacing rhythm consistent with nearby Oriana sections
- [ ] Mobile: nav, hero, forms, and CTAs usable at 375px
- [ ] Focus states and contrast meet WCAG AA for text/UI
- [ ] Reduced motion path works
- [ ] No layout shift from images/fonts (sizes reserved)
- [ ] Payload-driven content still renders; empty/error states are intentional
